```graphql
query ProductCard($id: ID!) {
  product(id: $id) {
    id
    name
    seller { name }
    reviews(first: 3) {
      rating
      summary
    }
  }
}
```

A successful result follows that selection:

```json
{
  "data": {
    "product": {
      "id": "P-42",
      "name": "Desk lamp",
      "seller": {"name": "Northwind"},
      "reviews": [{"rating": 5, "summary": "Easy to assemble"}]
    }
  }
}
```

The schema must define these fields and arguments, and the server must authorize and execute each selected part efficiently. The query's convenience does not guarantee one database query.
